@ [post_p2_readiness] docs/planning/Post_P2_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop

& [PostP3ReadinessSurfaceV1] is the current readiness surface after P3 compiled SOP operator contract acceptance
  + [surface_state] is ready_for_next_deeper_reasoning_design_selection
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is PostP2ReadinessSurfaceV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P3CompiledSOPOperatorContractsFinalSliceSurfaceV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P3OperatorBoundaryImportAndDutyInventoryV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P3CommonOperatorContractEnvelopeAndRefusalSemanticsV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P3SignatureValidationOperatorContractRefreshV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P3SupportReadinessRecomputeOperatorContractRefreshV1
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is P3OperatorTraceFixtureOracleAndNoAutomationBoundaryPlanV1
  + [active_implementation_chunk] is none
  + [current_ready_chunk] is P4 whole-field planning and packetization
  + [secondary_ready_chunk] is P5 LangGraph procedure runtime after P4 packetization contracts and fixture contracts advance
  + [gated_chunk] is P6 surface projection expansion until P4 and fixture records advance
  + [gated_chunk] is P8 fixture material creation until future source-preserved implementation activation explicitly opens files
  + [gated_chunk] is operator implementation until future source-preserved implementation activation explicitly opens operator code
  + [gated_chunk] is manager adapter, transport, UI, dependency, package metadata, and dispatch work until explicit non-live authority is accepted
  + [gated_chunk] is live-control authority reconsideration until separate source-preserved SJS authority is accepted
  + [safety_limit] is no dispatch, operations control, or live machine control authorized

  = must: choose the next slice from current support, completed-work deltas, and whole-field dependency closure
  = must: run completion review after each new design, planning, proof, or implementation slice before opening downstream slices
  = must: preserve P2 authority kernel overlays and P3 operator contract refusal, trace, nonpromotion, and no-automation boundaries
  = must: keep dispatch and live-control work blocked unless a separate future authority is source-preserved, SJS-processed, least-privilege bounded, rollback-proved, abort-proved, monitored, and accepted

& [ReadinessChunk: P4WholeFieldPlanningAndPacketization] is ready_for_slice_minting
  + [chunk_id] is P4
  + [chunk_name] is whole-field planning and packetization
  + [dependency_set] is P1 semantic authority and source lineage
  + [dependency_set] is P2 authority kernel and record schema refresh
  + [dependency_set] is P3 compiled SOP operator contracts
  + [expected_output_set] is source-preserved P4 final slice surface
  + [expected_output_set] is readiness-to-work-packet packetization contract
  + [expected_output_set] is completion review delta gate contract
  + [expected_output_set] is work packet generation no-dispatch boundary
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is packetization decides how readiness becomes work packets without assignment, dispatch, operations control, or live-control authority
  + [future_packet_fixture_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after P4 packetization template acceptance and bounded fixtures are defined
  + [forbidden_scope] is dependency installation, package metadata mutation, adapter implementation, transport implementation, UI implementation, command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent automation, operations control, and live machine control

  = must: keep work packets as reviewable records, not dispatch commands
  = must: require proof obligations, completion review, support delta, requirement delta, model route, forbidden scope, and no-live-effect notices on packetization contracts
  = must: route P4 slice minting through Specification Governance, Data Driven Design, and Feature Requirement Support because packetization consumes P2/P3 authority and changes downstream work readiness

& [PostP3OperatorContractStatus] is the accepted P3 status for downstream design
  + [operator_boundary_import_status] is accepted
  + [common_operator_envelope_status] is accepted_overlay
  + [signature_validation_refresh_status] is accepted_contract_only
  + [support_readiness_refresh_status] is accepted_contract_only
  + [fixture_oracle_status] is accepted_plan_only
  + [baseline_operator_files_status] is preserved_as_accepted_boundary_inputs
  + [operator_implementation_status] is not_authorized
  + [graph_node_implementation_status] is not_authorized
  + [packetization_status] is ready_for_P4_design_only

  = must: require downstream P4, P5, P6, and P8 planning to consume P3 outcome kinds, refusal kinds, trace rules, nonpromotion policy, and no-automation boundary explicitly
  = must: mark downstream designs stale if P3 source, operator envelope, operator refresh, fixture oracle, completion review, or this readiness surface changes

& [PostP3SafetyBoundary] is the safety boundary after P3 acceptance
  + [operator_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [LangGraph_node_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [fixture_source_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_ledger_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_database_creation_authorized] is false
  + [dependency_installation_authorized] is false
  + [package_metadata_mutation_authorized] is false
  + [adapter_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [transport_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [UI_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [manager_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [agent_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [job_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat P3 outputs as operator contract design authority, not runtime, graph, storage, adapter, dispatch, operations-control, or live-control authority
  = must: reject operator trace success, readiness success, fixture plan success, graph checkpoint state, generated output, mailbox carrier state, dry-run evidence, or human override as dispatch or live-control authority

& [PostP3ReadinessClosureReview] is the dependency audit for the post-P3 readiness surface
  + [P3-S01_status] is accepted
  + [P3-S02_status] is accepted
  + [P3-S03_status] is accepted
  + [P3-S04_status] is accepted
  + [P3-S05_status] is accepted
  + [P3_completion_status] is accepted_after_review
  + [current_ready_chunk_set] is P4 whole-field planning and packetization
  + [conditionally_ready_chunk_set] is P5 LangGraph procedure runtime after P4 and fixture contracts advance
  + [unresolved_external_dependency_set] is empty_after_gate
  + [forbidden_external_dependency_found] is false
  + [manager_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [agent_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat implementation activation, adapter work, transport work, dispatch authority, live-control authority, and downstream operations execution as gated, not ready
  = must: rerun closure review when a P3 boundary pack changes, proof fails, or operator contract contradiction appears
